    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "creating a story feels so... performative. like putting makeup on a corpse. it just feels like more noise, more effort spent on something that’s fundamentally hollow. why should i keep pretending that making up a \"small truth\" is any different from the lie i've been living for the last decade? it's just exhausting.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
